  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Acidifying barium peroxide and removing excess water by evaporation under reduced pressure gives hydrogen peroxide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></msub></math></p><p>This is a common method to prepare hydrogen peroxide</p>",
